# Underground Heist — first playable slice

## Host integration
Undertale remains the game being launched. The mod changes its flow by adding a heist encounter and returning control to the host game.

## First slice
Location: Underground / a new heist encounter attached to the existing Undertale flow.

Objective: perform a short vault-style heist with three phases:
- Infiltration: reach the objective without raising the alarm.
- Heist: interact with the objective while an escalating timer runs.
- Escape: reach the exit while enemies/pressure increase.

## PAYDAY elements
- Crew: Dallas, Chains, Wolf, Hoxton as selectable flavor/role presets.
- Equipment: armor/utility and deployable-style choices represented by Undertale-compatible mechanics.
- Alarm state: silent -> suspicious -> loud.
- Contract completion and escape result.

## Undertale elements
- Undertale dialogue boxes and encounter flow remain the presentation model.
- Existing player-owned Undertale content is used by the host rather than copied into this project.
- The mashup should preserve Undertale's movement/interaction feel while adding heist objectives.

## Multiplayer
Target: solo + cooperative play. This is not implemented yet. Do not claim a player limit or connection method until the project actually provides one and two-copy testing succeeds.

## First implementation target
Before adding the full crew/contract system, implement one complete contract end-to-end. This gives us a real gameplay slice to test and capture for the Melty listing.

